  "problem": "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nIn a beverage, there are $\\frac{2}{7}$ teaspoons of ginger for each teaspoon of sugar. Therefore, the beverage has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ teaspoons of ginger to $\\boxed{}$ teaspoons of sugar.",
  "worked_solution": "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{2}{7}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n2:7\n$$\n\nTherefore, the beverage has a ratio of $2$ teaspoons of ginger to $7$ teaspoons of sugar.",
